    `Father, I come to You this morning with the weight of what Your Son said about eternity pressing on me in a new way. I do not come in paralysing fear — but in the sober, reverential recognition that eternity is real, that its outcomes are permanent, and that the decisions being made every day by the people around me have consequences that extend infinitely beyond what any of us can see right now. I receive the warning of hell not as a weapon of manipulation but as the most serious expression of love available — the warning given by someone who knows what is coming and refuses to let those He loves walk into it without being told. Let that same love move in me. Let the urgency that caused Jesus to speak about this more than any other subject become an urgency in my own heart — for my own life, and for the people around me who have not yet made the decision that changes everything. I choose today to fear the right things. Not the things that can harm my body. The things that matter to eternity.`
